Record the human's approval of the brief, bound to its text; refused while `brief check` has blockers

Usage: canon brief approve [OPTIONS] --by <BY> --note <NOTE>

Options:
      --as <ROLE>              The role you act as: planner, implementer, reviewer or orchestrator. Overrides `CANON_ROLE`. `schema` lists the role's commands, `status` keeps its steps, and `--role` on `evidence add` / `review add` defaults to it [possible values: planner, implementer, reviewer, orchestrator]
      --by <BY>                Who approved (the human, not the agent)
      --note <NOTE>            The human's own words
      --change-id <CHANGE_ID>  The change to read (default: the repo's only live change)
      --repo <DIR>             The repo to act on (default: the nearest ancestor directory holding a canon.yaml)
      --json                   Output JSON instead of the human-readable form
  -h, --help                   Print help
  -V, --version                Print version

Examples:
  canon brief approve --change-id add-login --by Ana --note 'Go. Ship the failure flow too.'

Writes `Approved: <who> <when> — "<words>" (brief sha256:<digest>)` into the
brief (the digest covers the brief without its `Approved:` lines) and records
`canon policy approve` in the same call. Edit the brief afterwards and it reads as
not approved (BRIEF_CHANGED_SINCE_APPROVAL) until a human answers again and this
runs again. Run it only from the human's answer, with their words as --note.
